  "$comment": "GENESIS peoples on the LIVE sim (worker, scenario twoworlds): a band is set down from the test surface (life.spawn-people at the 'homestead' POI), walks, settles, builds; the god teaches fire; the settlement is followed over game days (camp -> huts -> fields -> paths), at night, in the inspector, and running at 100x with its news as toasts; then the live sim's bronze-age town and city (scenario lookdev on the worker) at night. All shots share one page (same URL), so they are one world's history. Waits are whole days (1440 ticks on Gaia: dayHours is the solar day since the phase-2 integration, so the sun comes back to the same hour every 1440 ticks). Run: node _harness/shots.mjs _harness/specs/peoples.json",
